 "name": "Man-At-Arms: Dwarven Armory",
 "notes": [
  "Nov 23, 2026 (later): middle kid's four picks (Gimli's Fury, Jhoira's Familiar, Path of Anger's Flame, Haunted Plate Mail) were tried in, then swapped back out pending a talk with him. Suggested home for Gimli's Fury if he wants it: cut Amber Gristle O'Maul instead of Hobbit's Sting.",
  "Nov 23, 2026: rebuilt as the best 99 from the Dwarf pile on hand tonight (127 cards). In: Bloodforged Battle-Axe, Gimli, Counter of Kills, Sting, Bilbo's Sword, +2 Plains. Out: Electrostatic Infantry (now in Gandalf), Brawler's Plate, Torch Gauntlet, -2 Mountains (13/13 split; white pips outnumber red). Left in the box: second copies (Erebor Flamesmith, Iron Hills Blacksmith, Thorin Oakenshield, Dwarven Shortsword, War of the Last Alliance), the other Erebor Flamesmith, Fiery Inscription, Glamdring (too few instants/sorceries), Mana Geyser, Hex Magic, Bull Rush, Path of Anger's Flame, Smaug's Fury, Gimli's Fury, Ranger's Firebrand, Jhoira's Familiar, Changeling Berserker, Haunted Plate Mail, 4 Mountains, 3 Plains.",
  "Nov 19, 2026: main list replaced with his actual sleeved deck, trimmed from 123 cards to 100. Removed 5 duplicates (Thorin Oakenshield, Iron Hills Blacksmith, Dwarven Shortsword, War of the Last Alliance, Erebor Flamesmith), 6 basics (40 to 34 lands), and 12 weak cards: the second Erebor Flamesmith, Fiery Inscription, Mana Geyser, Hex Magic, Bull Rush, Path of Anger's Flame, Smaug's Fury, Gimli's Fury, Ranger's Firebrand, Changeling Berserker, Jhoira's Familiar, Glamdring. The old Nov 3 build is saved as the 'Nov 3 plan' version.",
  "Upgrade path: Stage 1 (owned cards) → Stage 2 (about $4 of bulk Dwarves) → the 'adds' list (dollar-plus cards, cheapest first).",
  "With Bruenor out, every Equipment is +2/+0 on its own, so cheap junk Equipment is worth more here than pump spells.",
  "Check: the deck has a Nettlecyst; the three you've noted are in Doom Unrivaled, Winter Soldier and Black Panther. Sram and Puresteel Paladin are also in the Bucky deck.",
  "Commander is the Man-At-Arms printing of Bruenor Battlehammer: each creature gets +2/+0 per attached Equipment, and the first equip each turn is free."
 ],
